{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794050396,"nonce":"/nCH/XhgDEn+p6hBjKecMGUBrgo=","title":"Folding a Principal with passkeys needs a passkey of the folded Principal","message":"Whoever controls a user's forge login can fold that user's Principal into their own through `POST /v1/me/identities/link-moving-passkeys`. The folded Principal's role bindings and passkeys move to the attacker. The always-ask step-up proves a passkey of the surviving Principal, never the folded one.\n\nProposed: a merge that moves passkeys, or a Principal's bindings, also needs an assertion from one of the folded Principal's passkeys. Alternatively, never fold a Principal that holds passkeys.\n\nEvidence: safety A2 and red team RT-4 in ~/.afk/scrarab-ci/20261107-0247-decisions/review/. Reproduced by `a_link_moving_passkeys_always_asks_and_records_each_move` (crates/scarab-server/tests/step_up_redteam.rs). Needs an owner decision.","files":null}]}